 * S6-e2e unit 14 (Claude Sonnet 5.5) - vendor payout execution + history (T-802e75e8).
 *
 * Flow: vendor-a lists a product, a retail buyer buys and pays it (crypto_mock, settled via the sandbox
 * confirm route) so the vendor has a payable balance. The admin creates a PENDING payout for part of that
 * balance, executes it in manual mode (-> COMPLETED with the reference on the note), and reads it back
 * from GET /api/ledger/payouts/history. Also asserted: re-executing a COMPLETED payout is idempotent,
 * rail mode is refused for a vendor with no connected account (payout stays PENDING), non-admins get 403,
